01:10:34.570 --> 01:10:36.120
And then I'll communicate those

01:10:36.120 --> 01:10:37.510
with the author's here today.

01:10:37.510 --> 01:10:39.893
So let me turn it over to Al, go ahead Al.

01:10:42.140 --> 01:10:44.180
- Thank you so much for the presentation.

01:10:44.180 --> 01:10:45.290
Super, super fascinating.

01:10:45.290 --> 01:10:47.260
I think I was wondering where the tension

01:10:47.260 --> 01:10:48.950
on kind of building on a conversation

01:10:48.950 --> 01:10:50.000
about the future.

01:10:50.000 --> 01:10:51.940
So one way to look at it is the difference

01:10:51.940 --> 01:10:53.590
between (indistinct) and Pattana.

01:10:55.120 --> 01:10:57.130
So I think Leah, you wrote about that.

01:10:57.130 --> 01:10:59.210
In Lao, there's this
tension between progress

01:10:59.210 --> 01:11:00.450
and development.

01:11:00.450 --> 01:11:03.340
So like Lao people feel sometimes

01:11:03.340 --> 01:11:05.400
they don't have progress in the country.

01:11:05.400 --> 01:11:06.900
So is this kind of nationalist dialogue?

01:11:06.900 --> 01:11:08.890
So I'm wondering, like,
just kind of extending

01:11:08.890 --> 01:11:10.350
this conversation on temporalities?

01:11:10.350 --> 01:11:11.930
What is the kind of future

01:11:11.930 --> 01:11:13.875
of looking at a certain sense

01:11:13.875 --> 01:11:16.250
past the presentism?

01:11:16.250 --> 01:11:17.790
And rich kind of historicism?

01:11:17.790 --> 01:11:20.330
How do we reckon with what's going on?

01:11:20.330 --> 01:11:22.390
And think there's talk about land value

01:11:22.390 --> 01:11:23.223
and stuff like that?

01:11:23.223 --> 01:11:24.890
Just yeah, I'd love to hear a little more

01:11:24.890 --> 01:11:27.280
and maybe just potential speculation

01:11:28.150 --> 01:11:30.230
is there something
distinctive about the forest

01:11:30.230 --> 01:11:31.610
as opposed to the bomb landscape,

01:11:31.610 --> 01:11:32.780
as opposed to the ruins

01:11:32.780 --> 01:11:34.460
of the militarized zone sets?

01:11:34.460 --> 01:11:36.800
Are they kind of different
and distinct from each other,

01:11:36.800 --> 01:11:39.450
just kind of across the
different (Al laughing) yeah.

01:11:40.510 --> 01:11:41.343
Thank you.

01:11:43.953 --> 01:11:47.840
- I think what stood out
to be most in my research

01:11:47.840 --> 01:11:52.840
about Pattana was that
just like, pretty much

01:11:53.130 --> 01:11:54.840
everybody across the board didn't think

01:11:54.840 --> 01:11:56.790
it was possible in Laos.

01:11:56.790 --> 01:12:00.760
And I think that that's really
important ethnographically.

01:12:04.040 --> 01:12:05.810
That seems to me to just be an incredibly

01:12:05.810 --> 01:12:09.480
important evidence of like,
what widespread militarism

01:12:09.480 --> 01:12:11.460
does to a people's own impression

01:12:11.460 --> 01:12:15.850
of their possibility for a
future for a positive future

01:12:15.850 --> 01:12:20.850
that people have, cause
I hear it all the time.

01:12:22.050 --> 01:12:24.810
Like, oh, Laos doesn't have
the ability to do that.

01:12:24.810 --> 01:12:26.120
They could do that in Thailand,

01:12:26.120 --> 01:12:30.758
but we just can't do it
here. (Leah laughing)

01:12:30.758 --> 01:12:33.480
And in talking to other people,

01:12:33.480 --> 01:12:35.471
it was like a sort of catchphrase,

01:12:35.471 --> 01:12:38.270
it was just so common to
hear comments like this,

01:12:38.270 --> 01:12:40.917
like, "oh we're just
not capable of it here."

01:12:42.060 --> 01:12:44.786
And, if I push someone like, okay, well,

01:12:44.786 --> 01:12:48.590
why would it be possible
to have development

01:12:48.590 --> 01:12:50.993
in Cambodia, but not in Laos.

01:12:52.540 --> 01:12:54.380
People would give all
sorts of different answers.

01:12:54.380 --> 01:12:58.300
But I think the thread that
runs through all of them

01:12:58.300 --> 01:13:01.510
is this pervasive sense
that Laos is somehow

01:13:03.370 --> 01:13:05.470
kind of like a bucket with a hole in it.

01:13:05.470 --> 01:13:07.530
Like, it doesn't matter how much water

01:13:07.530 --> 01:13:10.200
you put in the bucket,
it's all gonna fall out.

01:13:10.200 --> 01:13:14.710
And that was not like the specific topic

01:13:14.710 --> 01:13:15.543
of my study.

01:13:15.543 --> 01:13:19.410
But I do think that that's
a really important feeling

01:13:19.410 --> 01:13:24.410
that is definitely
related to being targeted

01:13:24.900 --> 01:13:27.100
for a decade of covert warfare

01:13:27.100 --> 01:13:30.610
of massive covert warfare
that has never been adequately

01:13:30.610 --> 01:13:33.730
dealt with or acknowledged
by either the Lao government

01:13:33.730 --> 01:13:35.403
or the American government.

01:13:38.634 --> 01:13:40.563
- I'll attempt a response.

01:13:41.920 --> 01:13:44.810
Yeah, I think part of
what I've tried to do

01:13:44.810 --> 01:13:46.670
in my book is to lay out a method,

01:13:46.670 --> 01:13:48.700
I'm not sure how successful it is.

01:13:48.700 --> 01:13:51.180
But a method for understanding how people

01:13:51.180 --> 01:13:53.050
in a place like Vietnam,

01:13:53.050 --> 01:13:56.450
who have an understanding
of history, family history,

01:13:56.450 --> 01:14:00.300
place history that goes
back at least 400 years,

01:14:00.300 --> 01:14:03.683
if not an imagined history
that goes back longer.

01:14:04.570 --> 01:14:08.030
How they experience conflict
like the Vietnam War

01:14:08.030 --> 01:14:08.880
in the 60s.

01:14:08.880 --> 01:14:12.440
And my point is, though maybe
I should have revised it

01:14:12.440 --> 01:14:13.450
before I published the book

01:14:13.450 --> 01:14:16.630
is that it's fundamentally
different from Americans

01:14:16.630 --> 01:14:19.990
who are fighting after World
War Two, in these places.

01:14:19.990 --> 01:14:22.950
Who see it as a technical spot,

01:14:22.950 --> 01:14:25.810
thing on a map and improvise based city,

01:14:25.810 --> 01:14:28.200
and then they're gone and they leave it,

01:14:28.200 --> 01:14:31.763
except for the veterans who
still have the trauma of it.

01:14:32.880 --> 01:14:37.880
But I think that the
way that people develop

01:14:39.100 --> 01:14:41.610
the way development is understood

01:14:41.610 --> 01:14:45.630
in Vietnam is a kind of
schizophrenic experience

01:14:45.630 --> 01:14:46.463
in the sense.

01:14:46.463 --> 01:14:51.130
And I'm thinking about vast
acacia augustifolia plantations

01:14:51.130 --> 01:14:52.900
across the hills now,

01:14:52.900 --> 01:14:54.870
it used to be barren and you could see

01:14:54.870 --> 01:14:56.810
all the old base footprints.

01:14:56.810 --> 01:15:00.330
Now they're all covered up with
pulp and paper plantations.

01:15:00.330 --> 01:15:03.803
And the people who work in those places,

01:15:05.580 --> 01:15:09.470
the people who work in
it, they know the history.

01:15:09.470 --> 01:15:12.450
And when they're working
in those places, too,

01:15:12.450 --> 01:15:15.700
they're very much somehow
working through that history

01:15:15.700 --> 01:15:18.280
at the same time that
they're doing something new.

01:15:18.280 --> 01:15:19.870
And I think there's an understanding

01:15:19.870 --> 01:15:22.800
that part of your existence in a place

01:15:22.800 --> 01:15:24.820
like anywhere in Indochina,

01:15:24.820 --> 01:15:26.670
and most of Southeast Asia,

01:15:26.670 --> 01:15:30.740
is in a sense, defined by reconciling

01:15:30.740 --> 01:15:33.270
with this deeper past
and these deeper legacies

01:15:33.270 --> 01:15:35.880
and the ghosts around you.

01:15:35.880 --> 01:15:40.880
And the present sort of, churn
of earning a living working.

01:15:42.210 --> 01:15:45.300
And it's just a really
different experience.

01:15:45.300 --> 01:15:47.230
And that's what I'm trying
to convey in the book

01:15:47.230 --> 01:15:49.660
in the sense that if you read this book,

01:15:49.660 --> 01:15:51.550
you'll maybe get a little
better understanding

01:15:51.550 --> 01:15:54.780
of how Vietnamese combatant
might have felt or somebody

01:15:54.780 --> 01:15:57.890
in the Tet Offensive might
have felt, in this place.

01:15:57.890 --> 01:16:00.473
It's not just one layer, but it's deeper.

