01:16:16.630 --> 01:16:19.110
Well, this question of the
tension between progress

01:16:19.110 --> 01:16:22.143
and development that Al raised.

01:16:23.120 --> 01:16:24.560
When I set out to do field work,

01:16:24.560 --> 01:16:28.110
there was this narrative in this sort

01:16:28.110 --> 01:16:31.960
of development studies
literature that development,

01:16:31.960 --> 01:16:34.790
as a project was future oriented, right?

01:16:34.790 --> 01:16:38.450
So if you think about the book rule

01:16:38.450 --> 01:16:41.340
of experts by Tim Mitchell, right,

01:16:41.340 --> 01:16:44.010
Jim Scott's notion of high modernism,

01:16:44.010 --> 01:16:48.380
the idea was that the
imaginations of planners

01:16:48.380 --> 01:16:49.960
were all about imposing the will

01:16:49.960 --> 01:16:53.480
of the state, on the people
through an imagination

01:16:53.480 --> 01:16:57.213
of a technologically
superior, advanced future.

01:16:58.160 --> 01:17:01.370
And the question that I actually
had going into the field

01:17:01.370 --> 01:17:03.870
had to do with the ways in which arguments

01:17:03.870 --> 01:17:06.770
about development in
Cambodia are really arguments

01:17:06.770 --> 01:17:11.360
about the past, about
what the past authorizes.

01:17:11.360 --> 01:17:13.693
And in that case, landscape,

01:17:14.700 --> 01:17:16.690
certainly for the Jarai

01:17:16.690 --> 01:17:18.400
and for many people in Cambodia,

01:17:18.400 --> 01:17:19.710
the landscape that they live in

01:17:19.710 --> 01:17:23.550
it provides the material
with which to make claims

01:17:23.550 --> 01:17:25.220
on the past, right.

01:17:25.220 --> 01:17:27.740
Because the world that we live in,

01:17:27.740 --> 01:17:31.710
is formed by a traumatic
history of some sort.

01:17:31.710 --> 01:17:35.510
A traumatic history that
has a hard time moving back

01:17:35.510 --> 01:17:38.330
into the past because of
its utility in the present.

01:17:38.330 --> 01:17:41.020
So that even today, the first line

01:17:41.020 --> 01:17:43.880
of every development project document

01:17:43.880 --> 01:17:48.880
in Cambodia has to do with
the rupture of history

01:17:50.300 --> 01:17:53.323
that was created during
the Khmer Rouge period.

